# Documents tab, locked files, and e-sign

## Documents

- Uploads and Packets are one tab named **Documents**. E-Sign is the first
  section; uploaded files are the section under it. Collection letters stay in
  the uploads section, grouped by type (`collection_letter` or
  `is_collection_letter`).
- `?tab=letters` and `?tab=packets` both redirect to `?tab=documents`.

## Delete lock

- **Locked for everyone:** Collection Letter and POA (`poa_document`, `poa`,
  `poa_signed`, `power_of_attorney`).
- **Not locked:** CC Authorization (manual uploads). Signed e-sign files stay
  undeletable via `esign_requests`, including signed CC Auth.
- Enforce in the UI, `deleteOwnClientDocument` / `deleteClientDocument`, and RLS
  (`lock_permanent_client_document_deletes`). Check e-sign protection with the
  **service role**, not staff RLS.

## E-Sign

- The engine is CRM-native: tokenised `/sign/[token]` + OTP + SHA-256 +
  certificate of completion, with `pdf-lib` stamping and `pdfjs-dist` page
  rasterising. There is no third-party e-sign provider.
- Field placement is data-driven: percent-based boxes with a `bind` key from
  `ESIGN_BIND_KEYS`, placed by drag-and-drop in `EsignDocumentBoard` (mode
  `edit`) and saved as JSON. On upload, general labels (name, address, email,
  phone, date, signature, and similar) are suggested from the PDF text and
  saved as the starting placement. Staff still move, remove, and add the rest
  in the editor. Never go back to absolute-point field maps or a per-document
  hardcoded layout.
- `pdfjs-dist` is pinned to `3.11.174` with `canvas: false` aliased in
  `next.config.mjs`. Do not bump it opportunistically.
- Client `/sign/[token]` and `/api/sign/*` stay public (tokenised). Middleware
  must allow those paths **before** auth redirects.
- Client sign links use `publicAppUrl()` (`lib/constants/business-contact.ts`).
  Never hardcode an origin.
- Kill switch: `ESIGN_ENABLED=false`. Unset = **on**.
- Keep `send-invite-email.ts` spam-resistant: plain text + HTML, `reply_to`
  support, brand in the subject, no emojis or all-caps CTAs, visible site and
  full link.
- The signed Welcome Packet is stored as `poa_signed` and drives POA
  auto-advance. A signed CC authorization is what gates leaving Account
  Manager. CC Auth must **not** auto-stage. See
  `.cursor/rules/onboarding-stage-gates.mdc`.
- Confirm Before Sending is derived from the fields placed on that template
  intersected with `required_binds`. Empty required fields highlight. Client
  name stamps in Title Case. Account Manager is **first name only**, Title Case.
- A document is a row in `esign_templates`, owned by a MID. A client profile
  lists only that client's MID. Adding a MID and its PDFs is no-code: Settings
  → MIDs, upload, then place fields. Do not add a hardcoded document kind.
- Template PDFs live in the `esign-templates` storage bucket at
  `{midSlug}/{templateId}.pdf`. Nothing is bundled into the serverless
  functions. `lib/esign/templates/*.pdf` is only the Golden Pathway seed source.

## Attorney portal

- Do not drop `/api/clients/documents/download` from
  `ATTORNEY_PORTAL_API_ALLOWLIST`.
